+      "derivations": [
+        {
+          "id": "derivation-1.1",
+          "claim": "Let $z$ be a feasible iterate, $W$ its working set, and $u\\ne0$ the exact direction minimizer. Its KKT equation is $Bu+(Bz+c)+A^T\\nu+\\sum_{i\\in W}\\mu_iG_i^T=0$, with $Au=0$ and $G_iu=0$ for $i\\in W$. Multiplying by $u^T$ gives $(Bz+c)^Tu=-u^TBu$. Hence for every accepted $0<\\alpha\\le1$, $$q(z+\\alpha u)-q(z)=-\\alpha(1-\\alpha/2)u^TBu<0.$$ If $\\alpha<1$, a blocking row cannot lie in the span of the current rows, since it has $G_iu>0$ while every row in that span annihilates $u$; adding it preserves independence.",
+          "step": "1.1",
+          "inputs": [
+            "given",
+            "step 1.1",
+            "A1",
+            "F1",
+            "F2"
+          ]
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "derivation-1.2",
+          "claim": "Suppose instead $u=0$ and the multiplier of a working inequality $j$ is negative. After deleting $j$, let $v$ be the next exact direction. The new direction stationarity, dotted with $v$, gives $(Bz+c)^Tv=-v^TBv$. The old face stationarity, also dotted with $v$, gives $(Bz+c)^Tv+\\mu_jG_jv=0$, because all retained working rows annihilate $v$. Therefore $\\mu_jG_jv=v^TBv>0$, so $v\\ne0$ and $G_jv<0$. The dropped inequality is feasible to first order, and by the positive-step hypothesis the next iterate moves strictly along this descent direction.",
+          "step": "1.2",
+          "inputs": [
+            "given",
+            "step 1.2",
+            "A1",
+            "F1",
+            "F2"
+          ]
+        },
+        {
+          "id": "derivation-2.1",
+          "claim": "For a fixed working set $W$, positive definiteness makes the face objective have at most one minimizer. Once the algorithm reaches that face minimizer, either all working inequality multipliers are nonnegative and it terminates, or step 1.2 gives a strict objective decrease after a negative multiplier is dropped. Every later iterate is then below the minimum value on that face, so the same working set cannot be face-minimized again. There are at most $2^m$ working sets.",
+          "step": "2.1",
+          "inputs": [
+            "given",
+            "step 2.1",
+            "step 1.2",
+            "A1",
+            "step 1.1"
+          ]
