+          "id": "derivation-3.1",
+          "claim": "Between successive face minimizers, each nonterminal partial step adds an independent blocker, so there can be at most $n-r$ such additions before the feasible direction space is zero. A full step with no blocker reaches a face minimizer immediately. Thus each of the at most $2^m$ face-minimization episodes uses at most $n-r+2\\le n+2$ iterations. The cap $N\\ge(n+2)2^m$ cannot be reached before a terminal KKT point.",
