-   "derivations": [
-    {
-     "id": "derivation-1.1",
-     "claim": "The unit sphere is compact by [F4]. The continuous function $z\\mapsto z^TBz$ is positive on it, so it attains a positive minimum $\\alpha$. Thus $q(p)\\ge\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\|p\\|_2^2-\\|c\\|_2\\|p\\|_2$ by [F6], which tends to $+\\infty$ as $\\|p\\|_2\\to\\infty$. By [F1], the constraint rows are affine, so their closed half-spaces and affine equality sets intersect in a closed set; choosing one feasible $p_0$, the nonempty sublevel $\\{p\\in C:q(p)\\le q(p_0)\\}$ is bounded and closed, hence compact by [F4]. The minimum is attained there and therefore on $C$.",
-     "step": "1.1",
