-     "id": "derivation-1.1",
-     "claim": "Let $z$ be a feasible iterate, $W$ its working set, and $u\\ne0$ the exact direction minimizer. Its KKT equation is $Bu+(Bz+c)+A^T\\nu+\\sum_{i\\in W}\\mu_iG_i^T=0$, with $Au=0$ and $G_iu=0$ for $i\\in W$. Multiplying by $u^T$ gives $(Bz+c)^Tu=-u^TBu$. Hence for every accepted $0<\\alpha\\le1$, $$q(z+\\alpha u)-q(z)=-\\alpha(1-\\alpha/2)u^TBu<0.$$ If $\\alpha<1$, a blocking row cannot lie in the span of the current rows, since it has $G_iu>0$ while every row in that span annihilates $u$; adding it preserves independence.",
