-   "derivations": [
-    {
-     "id": "derivation-1.1",
-     "claim": "Write $A=A_*$, $H=H_*$ and $r=\\dim c$. Strict complementarity and continuity give a neighborhood in which every active inequality satisfies $\\lambda_i+\\rho g_i(x)>0$ and every inactive inequality, whose multiplier is initialized at zero, satisfies $\\lambda_j+\\rho g_j(x)<0$. On this branch, [F2] reduces the $x$-dependent augmented Lagrangian to $$\\Phi_\\rho(x,\\mu)=f(x)+\\mu^Tc(x)+\\frac\\rho2\\|c(x)\\|_2^2,$$ where $\\mu=(\\nu,\\lambda_I)$. Its gradient vanishes at $(x_*,\\mu_*)$.",
-     "step": "1.1",
